{"cwd": "/tmp/flyrig-sandboxes/20260725T064914/websearch-tool", "duration_ms": 7835, "hook_event_name": "PostToolUse", "permission_mode": "bypassPermissions", "prompt_id": "5222781b-75bb-406b-8177-75fd8cb5e5ab", "session_id": "<SESSION_ID>", "tool_input": {"query": "claude code hooks"}, "tool_name": "WebSearch", "tool_response": {"durationSeconds": 7.835649626999999, "query": "claude code hooks", "results": [{"content": [{"title": "Claude Code Hooks: A Practical Guide to Workflow Automation | DataCamp", "url": "https://www.datacamp.com/tutorial/claude-code-hooks"}, {"title": "GitHub - disler/claude-code-hooks-mastery: Master Claude Code Hooks · GitHub", "url": "https://github.com/disler/claude-code-hooks-mastery"}, {"title": "Claude Code hooks explained: the missing layer between prompts and production", "url": "https://joseparreogarcia.substack.com/p/claude-code-hooks-explained-the-missing"}, {"title": "Claude Code Hooks: Automate Your AI Coding Workflow", "url": "https://www.ksred.com/claude-code-hooks-a-complete-guide-to-automating-your-ai-coding-workflow/"}, {"title": "Claude Code Hooks Complete Guide — Automate and Enforce Rules Reliably - SmartScope", "url": "https://smartscope.blog/en/generative-ai/claude/claude-code-hooks-guide/"}, {"title": "Claude Code Hooks Complete Guide - Deterministic Enforcement Across the Tool Lifecycle | hidekazu-konishi.com", "url": "https://hidekazu-konishi.com/entry/claude_code_hooks_complete_guide.html"}, {"title": "Claude Code Hooks: Complete Guide to All 12 Lifecycle Events", "url": "https://claudefa.st/blog/tools/hooks/hooks-guide"}, {"title": "Claude Code hooks 是用户定义的 shell 命令,在 Claude Code 生命周期的各个点执行。Hooks 提供对 Claude Code 行为的确定性控制,确保某些操作总是发生,而不是依赖 LLM 选择运行它们。", "url": "https://docs.anthropic.com/zh-CN/docs/claude-code/hooks-guide"}], "tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_014HJdboXpRxTpzK3gqVVhaV"}, "Based on the search results, here's what Claude Code Hooks are:\n\n## Overview\n\nClaude Code Hooks are shell commands that run automatically when specific events happen during your AI coding session. Think of hooks like git hooks, but for your AI agent.\n\n## Key Purpose\n\nA hook is a user-defined command (or HTTP endpoint, or MCP tool, or sub-model evaluation) that Claude Code executes deterministically at a fixed point in the tool-and-conversation lifecycle. The critical distinction is that hooks inject deterministic processing into Claude Code's lifecycle. Unlike prompt instructions, which are requests that Claude may interpret flexibly, hooks execute the same way every time.\n\n## Common Use Cases\n\nClaude Code hooks automate coding tasks like testing, formatting, and receiving notifications. You can set up hooks for code formatting, test execution, notifications, and file protection.\n\n## How They Work\n\nA hook starts with an event, can optionally be narrowed with a matcher, receives structured input from Claude Code, and then executes one or more handlers. Configure them in .claude/settings.json (project) or ~/.claude/settings.json (global) using JSON with events, matchers, and commands.\n\n## Practical Advantage\n\nThe critical difference from prompt-based rules is that hooks are guaranteed to execute. If you set up a PreToolUse hook that blocks writes to .env files, it will always block them."], "searchCount": 1}, "tool_use_id": "toolu_01TQCBKeuh86A6qVA5BWvyuu", "transcript_path": "<TRANSCRIPT_PATH>"}
